/// New York State personal income tax.
///
/// Everyone who `lives us/ny` pays New York tax on top of federal tax. This
/// system reads `agi` from the federal tallies (New York starts from federal
/// adjusted gross income, the same tally), subtracts the New York standard
/// deduction and taxes the rest on the state brackets. Tax withheld or paid to
/// New York is credited to the year it is `for`, and what is left is owed by
/// April 15. New York City residents live in `us/ny/nyc`, which includes this
/// system.
///
/// Simplified on purpose: it leaves out itemized deductions, credits, the
/// New York differences from federal income and the tax benefit recapture on
/// high incomes. Only the `single` and `joint` filing statuses have figures.
///
/// SAMPLE DATA. The figures are community-maintained and were written from the
/// published tables, not checked against the Department of Taxation and
/// Finance. Verify them against the NY DTF (tax.ny.gov, "Tax rate schedule"
/// and the IT-201 instructions) before relying on them, and correct them in a
/// pull request when they are wrong.
system us/ny

use us


/// The New York State Department of Taxation and Finance.
entity dtf : government

/// New York income tax withheld from pay, or paid to the DTF directly. Every
/// arrival counts as New York tax already paid.
kind ny-tax : expense


/// Tax withheld from pay, or paid in installments, is credited against the tax
/// owed to New York for the year the payment is `for`. It is also a state tax
/// paid, which the federal return itemizes up to a cap.
///
/// To fix: send the payment to a place of kind `ny-tax`, and say what year it is
/// for with `for 2025`.
law credit-ny-payments
  on in
  when to is ny-tax
  count amount as ny-withheld
  count amount as salt
  when date > date(year, 12, 31)
  owe -amount to dtf by date(year + 1, 4, 15) as paid-after-year-end

/// New York State income tax for the year (Tax Law §601), on federal adjusted
/// gross income less the state standard deduction. Long-term gains are taxed as
/// ordinary income here. What was paid by the end of the year is set against
/// it, and the rest is owed by April 15 (Form IT-201). When more was paid than
/// is due, the amount is negative: a refund.
///
/// To fix: the brackets depend on `filing`: set `filing single` or `filing joint`
/// on the person or household that lives here.
law state-income-tax
  each year
  let taxable = max(tally(agi) - deduction[year, owner.filing], empty)
  count taxable as ny-taxable-income
  let liability = progressive(brackets[year, owner.filing], taxable)
  count liability as ny-income-tax
  owe liability - tally(ny-withheld) to dtf by date(year + 1, 4, 15) as ny-income-tax

// The marginal rate above each threshold (Tax Law §601). A year without a row
// uses the latest earlier one, so 2025 uses the 2024 rates. The 2026 rates
// are the first five lowered by a tenth of a point in the 2025 state budget.
// verify: the 2026 rows against the DTF's 2026 rate schedule.
param brackets
  2024 single          0 USD 4%    |      8_500 USD 4.5%  |     11_700 USD 5.25% |     13_900 USD 5.5%  |     80_650 USD 6%    |    215_400 USD 6.85% |  1_077_550 USD 9.65% |  5_000_000 USD 10.3% | 25_000_000 USD 10.9%
  2024 joint           0 USD 4%    |     17_150 USD 4.5%  |     23_600 USD 5.25% |     27_900 USD 5.5%  |    161_550 USD 6%    |    323_200 USD 6.85% |  2_155_350 USD 9.65% |  5_000_000 USD 10.3% | 25_000_000 USD 10.9%
  2026 single          0 USD 3.9%  |      8_500 USD 4.4%  |     11_700 USD 5.15% |     13_900 USD 5.4%  |     80_650 USD 5.9%  |    215_400 USD 6.85% |  1_077_550 USD 9.65% |  5_000_000 USD 10.3% | 25_000_000 USD 10.9%
  2026 joint           0 USD 3.9%  |     17_150 USD 4.4%  |     23_600 USD 5.15% |     27_900 USD 5.4%  |    161_550 USD 5.9%  |    323_200 USD 6.85% |  2_155_350 USD 9.65% |  5_000_000 USD 10.3% | 25_000_000 USD 10.9%

// The New York standard deduction (Tax Law §614).
param deduction
  2024 single  8_000 USD
  2024 joint  16_050 USD
